{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 58,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David. Do ye indeed speak righteousness, O congregation? do ye judge uprightly, O ye sons of men?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, in heart ye work wickedness; ye weigh the violence of your hands in the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked are estranged from their birth: they go astray as soon as they are born, speaking lies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their poison ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the poison of a serpent: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the deaf adder ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stoppeth her ear;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which will not hearken to the voice of charmers, charming never so wisely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Break their teeth, O God, in their mouth: break out the great teeth of the young lions, O LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them melt away as waters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " run continually: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he bendeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his bow to shoot",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his arrows, let them be as cut in pieces.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a snail ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " melteth, let ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every one of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pass away: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the untimely birth of a woman, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they may not see the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before your pots can feel the thorns, he shall take them away as with a whirlwind, both living, and in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.58.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.58.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that a man shall say, Verily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a reward for the righteous: verily he is a God that judgeth in the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
